wazuh Theory 


What is Wazuh?
Wazuh is an open-source SIEM and XDR platform used by Security Operations Centers (SOCs) to detect threats, monitor systems, collect logs, and respond to security incidents.

Wazuh Architecture
1. Wazuh Agent• Installed on endpoints (Windows, Linux, macOS)
• Collects logs, file integrity data, system events, and security information


• Wazuh Server (Manager)◇ Receives data from agents
◇ Applies detection rules
◇ Generates alerts


• Indexer◇ Stores and indexes security data for fast searching
• Dashboard◇ Web interface to view alerts, dashboards, and reports

Key Features
◇ Log collection and analysis
◇ File Integrity Monitoring (FIM)
◇ Intrusion Detection (HIDS)
◇ Malware detection
◇ Vulnerability detection
◇ Security Configuration Assessment (SCA)
◇ Rootkit detection
◇ Active Response (automatically block malicious activity)
◇ Compliance monitoring (PCI DSS, HIPAA, GDPR, CIS, NIST)


